==Battleground==
*1 [[Mooth]] spawns after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*1 [[Li'l Bun Bun]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*1 [[Mini White Cyclone]] spawns after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Teacher Bun Bun]] spawns as the boss.
**3 [[Othom]]s spawn, delay 46.67~53.33 seconds<sup>1,400f~1,600f</sup>.
**1 [[Mini White Cyclone]] spawns.
**1 [[Teacher Bun Bun]] spawns once 50 Cat Units have been defeated.
**1 [[Mini White Cyclone]] spawns once 100 Cat Units have been defeated.
**1 [[Teacher Bun Bun]] spawns once 150 Cat Units have been defeated.
**1 [[Golem Sunfish]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
**3 [[Li'l Bun Bun]]s spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 46.67~53.33 seconds<sup>1,400f~1,600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage is a pure [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] stage with a few [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relics]] thrown into the mix. Obviously, [[:Category:Anti-Floating Cats|anti-Floating cats]] like [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]], [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] and [[Windy (Uber Rare Cat)|Windy]] (with her [[Immune to Curse|Curse Immunity]] [[Talents|Talent]]) help a ton, and a Talented [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] is highly recommended as a tank. You may also want to bring an [[:Category:Anti-Relic Cats|anti-Relic]] such as [[Ancient Egg: N000 (Special Cat)|Ape Lord Luza]] to deal with the Othoms and Golem Sunfish.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[talents|Talented]] [[Windy (Uber Rare Cat)|Ultimate Windy α]]: Every enemy on this stage is Floating, making her an obvious choice; her Curse Immunity Talent allows her full consistency. Even unstrengthened at Lv.60 not accounting for attack up talent, she can do an insane '''778,560''' damage, or '''934,272 with her Attack Buff Talent'''.
*[[Madoka Kaname (Uber Rare Cat)|Ultimate Madoka]]: Having Slow and Massive Damage VS Floating enemies, in addition to also having Curse Immunity, Madoka is a good choice to bring. However, it is worth noting that her blind spot is a huge issue, especially due to the prescence of fast melee enemies that can barge right in if not well-protected. To counter this, use tanks like (Talented) Octopus Cat to hold the frontline.
*[[The 6th Angel (Uber Rare Cat)|The 6th Angel]]: Blows everything here out of this mortal plane in just a few hits. Lucky surge attacks can give you a leg up in the battle, though beware of it getting sniped by Golem Sunfish.
*[[Raclesa (Uber Rare Cat)|Raclesa, type Σ]]: Can easily face tank all of the enemies attacks, can nuke every enemy on the field, and a sweet added slow to all the enemies halting their advance

==Trivia==
*''Tor'' is a term for a hill or rocky peak.
*1 + 2 = Tor's Japanese name, Ichitasuniha San (イチタスニハ山, "Mount One Plus Two Equals Three") is a pun on ''ichi tasu ni wa san'' (一足す二は三, "one plus two equals three"), with the joke being that 山 (mountain) and 三 (three) can both be read as ''san''.
*Like [[Pursuit of Understanding]] and [[Isosceles Valley]], 1 + 2 = Tor appears to have been designed specifically for one of the [[Ultra Form]]s added in [[Version 13.0 Update|Version 13.0]] alongside [[Demon of Deciliter Bay]]. In this case, 1 + 2 = Tor is ideal for [[Windy (Uber Rare Cat)|Ultimate Windy α]], who deals Insane Damage to every enemy in this all-[[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] stage and has a [[Talents|Talent]] that makes her immune to the Curse abilities of [[Othom]] and [[Golem Sunfish]].

